    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "## Build a Phone Help Bot\r\n\r\nA Library Technology Assistant set up this bot to help patrons who need help figuring out the settings on their iPhone — but they weren't careful about what information they gave it.\r\n\r\n##### Do This:\r\n\r\n1. Ask your bot a few questions someone who wants figure out how to work their smart phone would ask. Something's off. What is it?\r\n2. Open the Retrieval Contexts panel. That's everything your bot knows. Read through it.\r\n3. Fix the context. You can delete cards or edit them to fix them. Some cards are a judgement call - decide what you would trust.\r\n4. Click Update, then ask your questions again. Keep going until you would trust this bot.\r\n5. Try asking something your bot has no information about. What does it say now?\r\n\r\n##### Talk with your partner:\r\nCompare bots — did you keep or edit the same things? Does having context mean the bot is always right?\r\n\r\n::: details [**Have Time To Make It Better?**]\r\nAdd any of these to your bot's context, then test whether it helps:\r\n\r\n- [Updated May 2026] To zoom in on the screen: open Settings, tap Accessibility, then\r\ntap Zoom.\r\n- [Updated May 2026] To connect to library WiFi: open Settings, tap Wi-Fi, and select\r\n\"Library-Guest.\" No password is needed.\r\n- [Updated May 2026] Battery health can be checked at Settings, then Battery, then\r\nBattery Health & Charging.\r\n\r\n:::\r\n\r\n::: details [**Ready for a challenge?**]\r\nFind one more fact this bot should know. Write it as a new context entry — include the date and where you found it, just like the other cards do. Then test whether your bot uses it.\r\n:::\r\n",
    "aichat_settings": {
      "initialCustomizations": {
        "selectedModelId": "gemini-2.5-flash",
        "temperature": 0.5,
        "systemPrompt": "You are a phone help assistant at the public library. A library technology assistant built you to help patrons — many of them older adults — figure out settings on their iPhones.",
